## Tests and quality

```bash
cmake -S . -B build -DXMPL100_BUILD_TESTS=ON && cmake --build build && ctest --test-dir build
```

The host tests run the driver against a model of the sensor's output and produce each error the driver can return.
A fuzzer fails conversions and returns any voltage, and checks the driver's promises after every call. CI also
builds for Cortex-M and gates coverage, complexity, sanitizers, fuzzing, clang-tidy, cppcheck and the handbook
rules (`.kokeb/handbook.yml`). See [Testing and CI](docs/testing.md), which lists every gate and its limit.

